{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:c46117215ce2e346","name":"Old Republic Brigadier","source":{"id":"source:reference-c46117215ce2e346","title":"Old Republic Brigadier","revision":19272,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:38:21Z","sha256":"1b91f14c78329553a270c3beddde87f391f22b68e810e2439401c7683b699e43","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19272","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Old%20Republic%20Brigadier&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-c46117215ce2e346","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic","referenceId":"reference:6517b7e15507b001"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Brigadier generals- known as \"Brigadiers\"- are the highest-ranking officers to see action in the Republic Armies from ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Great Sith War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Great_Sith_War"}," to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Mandalorian Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Mandalorian_Wars"},", so they are often the envy of their deskbound superiors.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["That said, Brigadiers rarely feel the envy of anyone, as they frequently have to contend with missions out of all proportion to the forces and material available. Crafty Brigadiers make do by encouraging their underlings to live off the land, bending- but rarely breaking- local Republic statutes to make sure the mission is accomplished.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Few Brigadiers excel in negotiating skills, a hindrance in dealing with the banes of their existence, the mercenary companies and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"}," militias they are often required to work with. Brigadiers so fear the headaches a promotion to general would entail that many famously sabotage their own careers- never in ways that harm their troops, but by saying or doing things that make them politically radioactive. As such, the longest-serving Brigadiers in ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic","referenceId":"reference:6517b7e15507b001"}," are a colorful bunch.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Old Republic Brigadier Statistics (CL 13)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 6/",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldier","referenceId":"reference:f826baa05bef6921"}," 5/",{"tag":"a","children":["Noble"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble","referenceId":"reference:190d375ec3483f8f"}," 3/",{"tag":"a","children":["Officer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Officer","referenceId":"reference:192135a8adabe174"}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 4\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +14; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +16\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, Bocce, Bothese, 3 Unassigned\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p"